  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 120 PM MDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nTransition to wetter weather starts to accelerate on Wed, as\nupper high center finally drifts into the srn plains and monsoon\nmoisture plume returns to Colorado. Greatest coverage of storms\non Wed will be over the mountains/valleys, with pockets of heavy\nrain possible as air mass moistens. Storms less numerous east of\nthe mountains, though swly steering flow should carry at least \na few storms eastward onto the plains Wed afternoon/evening. \nMountain max temps will cool several degf Wed as mid level temps\nfall and cloud cover becomes more widespread, while only minor \ncooling expected on the plains where readings could still exceed\n100f over the lower Arkansas Valley for one last day. High then\nslides into the sern U.S. for late week into the weekend, with \nmonsoon moisture well entrenched over Colorado through the \nperiod. Cold front late Wed/Thu will also bring back low level \nmoisture to the plains and eastern slopes. Expect widespread \nshowers and thunderstorms each day, with heavy rainfall and \nflash flooding possible as well. Temps will cool back into the \n70s/80s through the period, which will be a few degf under \nseasonal averages for a change.",
